---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';

const facts = [
  {
    term: 'education',
    value: profile.education.degree,
    sub: `${profile.education.school} · ${profile.education.period}`,
  },
  { term: 'focus', value: 'AI systems · ML · backend · computer vision' },
  { term: 'currently', value: 'building RAG apps & backend services' },
  { term: 'based in', value: profile.location },
];
---

<section id="about" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
  <SectionHeading title="About" />

  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.5fr_1fr]">
    <div data-reveal class="space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      <p>
        I recently finished my Computer Science degree at the {profile.education.school}, where I
        got hooked on how intelligent software
        <strong class="font-medium text-ink">actually works</strong>, not just how to call it.
        That curiosity runs both ways: I'll derive the mathematics behind attention, then turn
        around and ship an application on top of an LLM.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work I reach for sits where AI systems meet software engineering: retrieval pipelines
        taken from document loader to grounded answer, backend services that talk through message
        queues, and convolutional networks trained end to end in PyTorch.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the layers underneath: backpropagation, gradient descent, attention
        mechanics, database internals. Knowing the mechanism is what makes the abstraction
        trustworthy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside data-reveal style="--reveal-i: 1" class="h-fit border-l-2 border-line pl-6">
      <dl class="space-y-6">
        {
          facts.map((fact) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-3">
                {fact.term}
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-ink">{fact.value}</dd>
              {fact.sub && <dd class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-ink-2">{fact.sub}</dd>}
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
